# Every text file is LF in the working tree on every OS.
#
# Without this, git on Windows honours its default `core.autocrlf=true` and checks files out as
# CRLF. `src/__tests__/commands-doc.test.ts` compares a COMMITTED markdown file against renderer
# output, and the renderer emits LF - so that test failed on `windows-latest` only, twice, on
# main, immediately after the cli 0.39.0 release. The text was identical; the bytes were not.
#
# Verified safe when added: `git ls-files --eol` reported every tracked file as `i/lf`, so this
# renormalises nothing and is purely protective.
#
# The test normalises on read as well. Two layers on purpose: this one fixes the whole class for
# any future test that reads a committed file, and the in-test normalisation means the test does
# not depend on a contributor's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
